	(text "RC filter for SOA means a small low-pass filter before the MCU ADC to reduce PWM switching noise.\nConnect it like this:\nSOA → 100 Ω to 1 kΩ resistor → STM32 ADC pin\nThen from the ADC side of that resistor:\nSTM32 ADC pin → 1 nF to 4.7 nF capacitor → AGND/GND\nSame for SOB and SOC. The datasheet says SOA/SOB/SOC are current-sense outputs and can support a low-pass filter using a series resistor and capacitor to ground.\nA safe starting value is 1 kΩ + 1 nF. Do not use a huge capacitor, or your current reading becomes too slow.\nCP is the charge-pump output. It is used internally by the DRV8316 to drive the high-side MOSFET gates. You do not power anything from it. Connect 1 µF from CP to VM, placed close to the chip. Also connect 47 nF between CPH and CPL. The datasheet specifies CP as charge-pump output and CPH/CPL as charge-pump capacitor pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 72.39 175.006 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7e907e9d-a514-4681-a003-3b68befbf522")
	)
